  "description": "The WHEN 'N' OR 'n' arm of SUBMIT-JOB-TO-INTRDR's ordered EVALUATE at :480-483, the middle of its three arms. The operator declines: INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS blanks the ten input items and clears WS-MESSAGE at :646, :482 raises the error flag and :483 sends an EMPTY form with no message at all. Nothing is emitted, and the reason is worth stating precisely - :496 still sets END-LOOP-NO and the PERFORM VARYING at :498 is still reached, but its UNTIL already holds because of ERR-FLG-ON, so the body runs zero times. The monthly arm ran to completion first, so the four PARM- fields hold 2026-08-01 and 2026-08-31; they are simply never written anywhere, which is why this case pins no record. Expected values are STATICALLY DERIVED by reading app/cbl/CORPT00C.cbl, its copybooks, app/bms/CORPT00.bms and app/csd/CARDDEMO.CSD - never captured from a COBOL run, which is impossible in this environment (risk R-A). Java has no transient data queue, so EXEC CICS WRITEQ TD QUEUE('JOBS') at :517 is reproduced through an explicit job-submission port; the eighty-byte content is identical and the dataset key JOBS names the TDQUEUE(JOBS) that app/csd/CARDDEMO.CSD:499-505 defines as RECORDSIZE(80) RECORDFORMAT(FIXED) BLOCKFORMAT(UNBLOCKED) DISPOSITION(MOD).",
